@namespace NoBorders.Components.Screens
@* Phase 8.6: replaces the old static/single "Center On Monitor" text link
   (DisplayDetailPane) and its Phase 8.5 copy (MonitorsSettingsPage) with
   four icon buttons — one per MonitorAlignMode. Shared here since both
   pages need the identical icon/markup/style four times each rather than
   duplicating the SVG.

   Icon and interaction states came out of a live mockup round (align_buttons
   candidates A/B/C/D): a small monitor-outline + filled-window-rect diagram,
   positioned per Position, drawn with `currentColor` for both shapes so the
   button's own CSS `color` drives the icon tint through every state —
   quiet at rest, MonitorAlignButton.razor.css's :hover lifts it (Candidate
   A's field→raised/border→border-strong pair) to signal it's clickable, and
   :active flashes Candidate A's .is-active palette (accent border/tint/icon)
   for the click instant, since these are one-shot actions, not a persisted
   selection.

   review.md §4.3: was a <div @onclick>, not in the keyboard tab order and
   with no accessible name exposed to assistive tech (title alone is
   unreliable — invisible until hovered, and many screen readers don't
   announce it). Now a real <button> with aria-label="@Title"; title stays
   too, for the visible hover tooltip sighted mouse users already get. *@

<button type="button" class="nb-align-btn" title="@Title" aria-label="@Title" @onclick="() => OnClick.InvokeAsync()">
    <svg width="20" height="15" viewBox="0 0 32 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <rect x="1" y="1" width="30" height="22" rx="3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" />
        <rect x="@WindowX" y="@WindowY" width="14" height="10" rx="1.5" fill="currentColor" />
    </svg>
</button>

@code {
    [Parameter] public MonitorAlignMode Position { get; set; } = MonitorAlignMode.Center;
    [Parameter] public string Title { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClick { get; set; }

    private int WindowX => Position switch
    {
        MonitorAlignMode.Left  => 2,
        MonitorAlignMode.Right => 16,
        _                      => 9, // Center, Bottom
    };

    private int WindowY => Position == MonitorAlignMode.Bottom ? 12 : 7;
}
